        'After about 10 minutes, when the coffee cools a little, it is tasted with a spoon, slurping hard to spread the liquid around the mouth. Aroma, sweetness, acidity, body, balance and aftertaste, what remains after swallowing, are evaluated. Coffees get scores, and those with 80 points or more are considered specialty.',
