        'After roasting, coffee goes through three phases. In the first days it releases a lot of gas and still tastes a bit green. Between one and three weeks it reaches its best point: aromatic, sweet and balanced. After about a month it starts to lose aroma and turn dull. Ground, this happens in minutes, which is why grinding on the spot is ideal.',
